0","id":472723,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MjcyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/472723?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RC-1290","html_url":"https://github.com/RC-1290","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RC-1290/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RC-1290/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RC-1290/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RC-1290/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RC-1290/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RC-1290/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RC-1290/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RC-1290/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RC-1290/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-09T11:43:22Z","updated_at":"2025-07-09T11:43:22Z","body":"It looks to me like the texture array used by the viewport is never written to at all, when using OpenXR.\n(Rather than being cleared, or being accessed at the wrong time). \n\nAt least that's the difference I'm noticing between an OpenXR project and the provided teststereo project, when I look at them in RenderDoc. It looks to me like in the teststereo project, the textureArray gets written to with something like the tonemap.glsl shader. That last bit may not be relevant, because tonemapping does still get applied to the images seen in the HMD.\n\nInitially I tried to figure it out from the Godot source code, but I did not yet manage to understand where the viewport texture is supposed to get written to, or looking from the other direction: where the link is supposed to be made between the viewport's texture storage and the rendering code in RendererSceneRenderRD::render_scene. I don't know whether I'm not finding that link because of a lack of understanding of how the rendering servers work, or because the link is actually missing.\n\n(I've been looking into this a little bit because I wanted a low-overhead screen-mirror for the spectator screen, and because I figured it might help me become more familiar with Godots rendering internals. You may assume I don't know what I'm talking about yet.)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3052322311/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3216004673","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100004#issuecomment-3216004673","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100004","id":3216004673,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_sFZB","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-23T00:26:44Z","updated_at":"2025-08-23T00:26:44Z","body":"@RC-1290 that sounds like the ViewportTexture isn'